# Code of Conduct

## Our Commitment

Raidcore is first and foremost a community built around shared interests, goals, and values. We strive to maintain an environment that is welcoming, constructive, and respectful for everyone involved.

We expect all contributors, maintainers, users, and community members to act with integrity, consideration, and common sense. Participation in Raidcore projects and communities is a privilege, and everyone is expected to uphold the principles outlined in this Code of Conduct.

We recognize that conduct outside our projects and platforms can also affect the organization and its community. We therefore reserve the right to take appropriate action in response to behavior outside these spaces when it has a meaningful impact on Raidcore, its projects, or its members.

## Our Principles

### 1. Treat Others with Respect

Be a decent person and treat others with dignity and respect. Harassment, threats, discrimination, personal attacks, and other abusive behavior will not be tolerated.

Do not engage in slander, targeted harassment, or public witch-hunts. Disagreements are inevitable, but they should never become personal or hostile. Report behavior that violates these principles rather than escalating it.

### 2. Engage in Good Faith

We encourage open discussion, constructive criticism, and respectful disagreement. Different perspectives and approaches are valuable, provided they are expressed in good faith.

Criticize ideas, implementations, and decisions rather than the people behind them. Be willing to explain your reasoning, consider alternative viewpoints, and acknowledge when you may be mistaken.

### 3. Seek Constructive Resolutions

Not every disagreement can be avoided, and misunderstandings will happen. What matters is how we respond to them.

Consider how your words and actions may affect others. Recognize when a joke or comment has gone too far and take responsibility when necessary. When conflicts arise, make a reasonable effort to resolve them constructively rather than escalating or prolonging them.

### 4. Be Welcoming and Encourage Learning

Raidcore projects should be accessible to people of varying experience levels. Welcome newcomers, encourage learning, and be willing to share knowledge.

Do not gatekeep, foster exclusionary cliques, or discourage participation based on someone's experience, skill level, or background. Constructive feedback should help people improve, not discourage them from contributing.

### 5. Create with Integrity and Respect

Develop and contribute to projects responsibly. Do not create, distribute, or knowingly support tools or modifications intended to provide unfair advantages over other players or otherwise undermine the integrity of the games and communities we support.

When collaborating with other developers, respect their work, contributions, and intellectual property. Be transparent, give appropriate credit, and approach collaboration in a professional and considerate manner.

## Enforcement

Violations of this Code of Conduct may result in appropriate corrective action, depending on the nature and severity of the incident.

Raidcore reserves the right to remove contributions, restrict participation, or revoke access to its projects and communities when necessary. Serious or repeated violations may result in permanent exclusion.

Enforcement decisions are made at the discretion of the Raidcore Team. We reserve the right to address conduct that occurs outside our platforms when it meaningfully affects Raidcore, its projects, or its community.

## Reporting

If you experience or witness behavior that violates this Code of Conduct, please report it to the Raidcore Team.

Reports can be submitted through GitHub or by emailing [contact@raidcore.gg](mailto:contact@raidcore.gg).

Please include relevant details and supporting information where possible. Reports will be handled with appropriate discretion, and we will make reasonable efforts to review and address them.

We expect everyone to cooperate in good faith when addressing reported incidents.
